-- title:
--   Generic étaleness of level sets over a local base
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local ring and $A$ a commutative $R$-algebra of finite presentation, all in one fixed universe, and assume the fibre $\kappa(R) \otimes_R A$ over the residue field of $R$ is an integral domain. Let $f \in A$ and let $m$ be a natural number whose image in $R$ is a unit. For a commutative local $R$-algebra $S$ and $s \in S$, write $B_{S,s} = (S \otimes_R A)/(1 \otimes f - s \otimes 1)$ for the quotient by the ideal generated by that single element, the level set of $f$ at the value $s$. Assume that for every such $S$ and every $s \in S$ the $S$-module $B_{S,s}$ is finite and free of rank $m$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a polynomial $D \in R[X]$ having at least one coefficient that is a unit of $R$, such that for every commutative local $R$-algebra $S$ whose structure map $R \to S$ is a local homomorphism and every $s \in S$ with $D(s)$ a unit in $S$, the $S$-algebra $B_{S,s}$ is étale.
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra core of the assertion that almost all level sets of a function are étale, a one-function Bertini statement over a local base: the non-étale values of $s$ are confined to the zero locus of a single polynomial $D$ with a unit coefficient. It is used by the corresponding statement for smooth proper curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_exists_polynomial_isUnit_aeval_imp_etale_levelSet.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u

open scoped TensorProduct
open Polynomial

theorem Algebra.exists_polynomial_isUnit_aeval_imp_etale_levelSet
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] [Algebra.FinitePresentation R A]
    [IsDomain (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R ⊗[R] A)]
    (f : A) (m : ℕ) (hm : IsUnit (m : R))
    (hls : ∀ (S : Type u) [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalRing S] (s : S),
        Module.Finite S (S ⊗[R] A ⧸ Ideal.span {(1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R] f - s ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)}) ∧
        Module.Free S (S ⊗[R] A ⧸ Ideal.span {(1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R] f - s ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)}) ∧
        Module.finrank S (S ⊗[R] A ⧸ Ideal.span {(1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R] f - s ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)}) = m) :
    ∃ D : Polynomial R, (∃ i, IsUnit (D.coeff i)) ∧
      ∀ (S : Type u) [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalRing S] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)] (s : S),
        IsUnit (Polynomial.aeval s D) →
        Algebra.Etale S (S ⊗[R] A ⧸ Ideal.span {(1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R] f - s ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)}) := by sorry
